om/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 05-26-2023, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T02:40:28-07:00","id":1512847,"title":"","content":"Wuhu! I have kept an eye out for this one ever since I heard that it is being developed!<br /> <br /> Really really excited for this! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Looks like christmas is coming early this year /o/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T08:14:03-07:00","id":1512874,"title":"","content":"I wrote on this (two Dark Eras, actually!) and Sam gave me his dark blessing to share a little tease from our massive Dark Eras of Rome chapter, from one of the two I worked on.<br /> <br /> I hope this intrigues you enough to begin with:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Even in their eternal stagnation, the Propinqui sense the war with Carthage holds more than meets the eye. Against it, the Republic finds its greatest challenge yet, and so does the Camarilla. Its members stand aghast as a dark truth slowly reveals itself, whisper after whisper: Not unlike Rome, Carthage holds its own society of predators within its walls. In the tongue of their people, these dead call themselves \u201cLords,\u201d a word Roman vampires hesitate to pronounce out loud: </i>Baali<i>.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I wrote about Carthage for one of my eras and did something I'm very, very proud of, hehe.<br /> <br /> (Also proud of my other Dark Era, but for different, explosive reasons)\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T09:38:47-07:00","id":1512882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1512810-requiem-for-rome-second-edition-coming-may-31st?p=1512874#post1512874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wrote on this (two Dark Eras, actually!) and Sam gave me his dark blessing to share a little tease from our massive Dark Eras of Rome chapter, from one of the two I worked on.<br /> <br /> I hope this intrigues you enough to begin with:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Even in their eternal stagnation, the Propinqui sense the war with Carthage holds more than meets the eye. Against it, the Republic finds its greatest challenge yet, and so does the Camarilla. Its members stand aghast as a dark truth slowly reveals itself, whisper after whisper: Not unlike Rome, Carthage holds its own society of predators within its walls. In the tongue of their people, these dead call themselves \u201cLords,\u201d a word Roman vampires hesitate to pronounce out loud: </i>Baali<i>.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I wrote about Carthage for one of my eras and did something I'm very, very proud of, hehe.<br /> <br /> (Also proud of my other Dark Era, but for different, explosive reasons)\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Elton John Voice: the Baali is back!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T11:16:35-07:00","id":1512894,"title":"","content":"None More Dark Publishing keeps the Requiem's flame alive. I am looking forward to reading your take on Requiem for Rome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T13:26:34-07:00","id":1512906,"title":"","content":"One of the writers, reporting in! I handled the Lancea et Sanctum, Cult of Augurs, the Blood Sorcery rehaul and new rites, and the mechanical parts of the Strix section! I'm looking forward to seeing what everyone thinks of the book, I think the team knocked it out of the park. I don't think I have much to say for now unless anyone has questions (keep in mind I'm still technically under an NDA!) but I'll drop by to explain some of my design rationale for the sections whenever they come up in previews. Then I will have a <i>lot</i> to say since there's quite a bit of crunch to go through...and the Strix and L&amp;S have some new fluff that I hope will make for good story seeds.\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raziel MacPhereson, he/they | <a href=\"http://twitter.com/beastsoulfury\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a> | <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Raziel%20MacPhereson\" target=\"_blank\">STV Content</a> | <a href=\"https://huntunderironskies.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Tumblr</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23812-cherubic","name":"Cherubic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23812_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T15:25:52-07:00","id":1512917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cherubic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1512810-requiem-for-rome-second-edition-coming-may-31st?p=1512906#post1512906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the writers, reporting in! I handled the Lancea et Sanctum, Cult of Augurs, the Blood Sorcery rehaul and new rites, and the mechanical parts of the Strix section! I'm looking forward to seeing what everyone thinks of the book, I think the team knocked it out of the park. I don't think I have much to say for now unless anyone has questions (keep in mind I'm still technically under an NDA!) but I'll drop by to explain some of my design rationale for the sections whenever they come up in previews. Then I will have a <i>lot</i> to say since there's quite a bit of crunch to go through...and the Strix and L&amp;S have some new fluff that I hope will make for good story seeds.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>How does the cult of Augurs see Jupiter Mars and the other gods? What are Jupiter and Mars and the other gods to them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T16:39:46-07:00","id":1512925,"title":"","content":"Funny thing you should mention vampires encountering the gods.<br /> <br /> [Redacted]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T16:49:41-07:00","id":1512926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1512810-requiem-for-rome-second-edition-coming-may-31st?p=1512925#post1512925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny thing you should mention vampires encountering the gods.<br /> <br /> [Redacted]</div> </div> </div> </div>Redacted,the god Redaction","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T08:27:15-07:00","id":1512962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1512810-requiem-for-rome-second-edition-coming-may-31st?p=1512917#post1512917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does the cult of Augurs see Jupiter Mars and the other gods? What are Jupiter and Mars and the other gods to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I don't want to steal Sam's thunder and spoil the previews, but I'll try to give a very quick teaser. Unless something changed a lot in the finals I would say for the average member their relationship with any god/s is going to be extremely transactional. There's a natural hierarchy to the universe and the gods (or something that might as well be gods, call them whatever you want as long as you're paying them their due respect) are at the top of it. The Cult of Augurs has a very mechanical way of seeing the world and the gods aren't an exception to that philosophy.<br /> <br /> Sorry for taking a bit! I had to think about how to say something without saying too much but I don't think the above will be a huge shock to anyone who's familiar with 1e. The Lancea et Sanctum, however, might've been refocused slightly...\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raziel MacPhereson, he/they | <a href=\"http://twitter.com/beastsoulfury\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a> | <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Raziel%20MacPhereson\" target=\"_blank\">STV Content</a> | <a href=\"https://huntunderironskies.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Tumblr</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23812-cherubic","name":"Cherubic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23812_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T15:30:55-07:00","id":1513010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cherubic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1512810-requiem-for-rome-second-edition-coming-may-31st?p=1512962#post1512962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, I don't want to steal Sam's thunder and spoil the previews, but I'll try to give a very quick teaser. Unless something changed a lot in the finals I would say for the average member their relationship with any god/s is going to be extremely transactional. There's a natural hierarchy to the universe and the gods (or something that might as well be gods, call them whatever you want as long as you're paying them their due respect) are at the top of it. The Cult of Augurs has a very mechanical way of seeing the world and the gods aren't an exception to that philosophy.<br /> <br /> Sorry for taking a bit! I had to think about how to say something without saying too much but I don't think the above will be a huge shock to anyone who's familiar with 1e. The Lancea et Sanctum, however, might've been refocused slightly...\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a really good summary of how things work! The Augurs are very matter of fact about religion, sort of weird philosophical naturalists.<br /> <br /> And speaking of the Lancea et Sanctum, if you all head over to the RPG.net thread, there might be a little something about them...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T19:09:01-07:00","id":1513030,"title":"","content":"I apologize for not understanding Yossarian, but what is the relationship the lancea et sanctum has with the Camarilla in this time period? I've never read requiem for Rome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T19:41:41-07:00","id":1513032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1512810-requiem-for-rome-second-edition-coming-may-31st?p=1513030#post1513030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize for not understanding Yossarian, but what is the relationship the lancea et sanctum has with the Camarilla in this time period? I've never read requiem for Rome</div> </div> </div> </div>In a word, complicated. The Lancea et Sanctum is much like the early Christian Church, in that it's persecuted frequently. However, the Witnesses are far more overtly hostile to the Camarilla. Of course, as time goes by and Rome Christianizes, the Sanctified gain a lot of power in the All Night Society, and eventually are the last ones standing when the Julii bite the dust, with the other wings scattering to the winds and taking on different forms in the dark medieval.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T20:21:36-07:00","id":1513033,"title":"","content":"Gotcha, so they are tolerated at best by the Camarilla guessing? Sorry about the further questioning. Since the camarilla is more centralized than covenants are, I assume they'd have more concerted efforts against vampire organizations they dislike","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T20:28:11-07:00","id":1513034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1512810-requiem-for-rome-second-edition-coming-may-31st?p=1513033#post1513033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotcha, so they are tolerated at best by the Camarilla guessing? Sorry about the further questioning. Since the camarilla is more centralized than covenants are, I assume they'd have more concerted efforts against vampire organizations they dislike</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Camarilla conducts official pogroms against the Sanctified early on (often mirroring mortal persecutions of Christians). This is something the Sanctified won't forget in later years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T21:12:19-07:00","id":1513035,"title":"","content":"Gotcha! Thank you for your patience","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T09:33:10-07:00","id":1513084,"title":"","content":"Hi wow I haven't been here in a while huh?<br /> I didn't contribute any writing, so I'm just as curious to see what's inside this book as everyone else, but I did do some bloodline art again! I now know more about ancient Roman shoes than I ever thought I would.<br /> Very excited to see how this all comes together, because, wow 300 pages is a lot! \ud83d\udc40","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T11:57:42-07:00","id":1513096,"title":"","content":"any chance you will be covering Nero's era?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1637-zen","name":"zen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T12:40:18-07:00","id":1513101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1512810-requiem-for-rome-second-edition-coming-may-31st?p=1513096#post1513096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">any chance you will be covering Nero's era?</div> </div> </div> </div>A smidge! We talk about it mostly in the context of the Year of the Four Emperors, briefly covering why Nero was unpopular among the patricians, how be died, and things like the Great Fire of Rome and the Pisonian Conspiracy. The Great Fire is kind of a turning point for the Kindred, so we wanted to provide a bit of coverage to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T15:25:13-07:00","id":1513123,"title":"","content":"I am very interested in this book, especially in the presentation of the Cult of Augurs (they are among my favorite &quot;Covenants&quot;). I hope that Veneficia will not be just folded into Cruac, but regardless I'm interested in this update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T15:59:35-07:00","id":1513130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1512810-requiem-for-rome-second-edition-coming-may-31st?p=1513123#post1513123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very interested in this book, especially in the presentation of the Cult of Augurs (they are among my favorite &quot;Covenants&quot;). I hope that Veneficia will not be just folded into Cruac, but regardless I'm interested in this update.</div> </div> </div> </div>I particularly can't give specifics about mechanics, but even while Blood Sorcery in general got tinkered with to make it a little more straightforward Veneficia is treated as a separate thing and has an aspect that would not transfer over well at all to Cruac. It's a little too...Vaticinator-y.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raziel MacPhereson, he/they | <a href=\"http://twitter.com/beastsoulfury\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter</a> | <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Raziel%20MacPhereson\" target=\"_blank\">STV Content</a> | <a href=\"https://huntunderironskies.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Tumblr</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23812-cherubic","name":"Cherubic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23812_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T16:27:39-07:00","id":1513133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1512810-requiem-for-rome-second-edition-coming-may-31st?p=1513123#post1513123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very interested in this book, especially in the presentation of the Cult of Augurs (they are among my favorite &quot;Covenants&quot;). I hope that Veneficia will not be just folded into Cruac, but regardless I'm interested in this update.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, it does use the basics of Cruac, but as Cherubic says, there are elements that wouldn't translate to Cruac. There's shared DNA, but there's definitely a different flavor, to completely mix my metaphors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T16:32:57-07:00","id":1513134,"title":"","content":"I must confess some interest in the mention of errata for the core system \u2014 obviously it's been about a decade since Blood &amp; Smoke, and the Contagion Chronicle PG was pretty up-front about some of the shifts in design sensibilities as the Revised Storytelling System rolled out, but can you speak to any particulars or generalities that the errata are for, aside from streamlining the Strix and blood sorcery mechanics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T18:28:36-07:00","id":1513142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1512810-requiem-for-rome-second-edition-coming-may-31st?p=1513134#post1513134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must confess some interest in the mention of errata for the core system \u2014 obviously it's been about a decade since Blood &amp; Smoke, and the Contagion Chronicle PG was pretty up-front about some of the shifts in design sensibilities as the Revised Storytelling System rolled out, but can you speak to any particulars or generalities that the errata are for, aside from streamlining the Strix and blood sorcery mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly just little clarifications; nothing revelatory, but I wanted to address some of the more nagging issues that have come up over the years in Vampire specifically and the RSS in general. Mostly its collating some of the stuff that's changed since Requiem 2E was published, mixed in with a few judgment calls. One thing in particular was putting all the ghoul family rules in one place, as they're kind of scattered between VTR and Half-Damned, and a little vague at that. The only thing I really straight-up changed is how you learn out-of-clan proprietary Disciplines; it's not <i>that</i> different, but it's ever so slightly less restrictive, and potentially adds an interesting story element to seeking them out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/ma